{
  "analysis": "The review describes a chance-based prize wheel in the genie game. The wheel appears to stop on a valuable reward, but the genie then redirects it to another spin, after which the reward is reduced from 100 million with a 5x multiplier to 48 million. This explicitly alleges that the game manipulates or conceals the determination of the outcome, supporting Illusion of Control. The wheel also uses an unpredictable spin-based reward delivery system, supporting Reward Mania. Although the game is a casino-themed title, the review does not explicitly describe real money being wagered or spent, so Gambling is not assigned.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_IllusionOfControl",
      "span": "the wheel spin after stopping on a great price the genie move the wheel to a spin tag, and then the prices after the spin are way lower than the original price",
      "rule_applied": "Boundary rule vs Alleged rigging: the span asserts that the game manipulates the determination of the wheel's outcome after it has apparently stopped.",
      "rationale": "The reviewer alleges that the game redirects an apparent winning result into a lower-value outcome, indicating manipulated or hidden outcome determination."
    },
    {
      "label": "P_RewardMania",
      "span": "the wheel spin after stopping on a great price",
      "rule_applied": "Variable Rewards / spin-wheel indicator: the reward is delivered through an unpredictable chance-based wheel mechanism.",
      "rationale": "The game sustains engagement through a spin wheel whose outcome determines the prize delivered."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes player-versus-player competition, with opponents commonly using Mega Knight, P.E.K.K.A., and Golem decks after 8k trophies. It also explicitly describes a pay-to-win design, claiming that advancing is not possible through skill alone and that the game is becoming more pay to win through updates. The complaints about annoying card spam and disliked card buffs describe balance and strategy frustrations, but they do not establish anti-social incentives, power creep of purchased items, or hidden outcome manipulation.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "its also pay to win",
      "rule_applied": "Pay to Win indicator under M_PayToProgress",
      "rationale": "The reviewer explicitly characterizes the game as pay to win, indicating that spending money grants an in-game advantage."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "all you play against after 8k trophies is mega knight,pekka, and golem",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The span describes competing against other players whose decks use these cards."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a purchasable Fishdom pass, which the permitted search identified as a season/gold pass, so the pass mechanic is codable as Recurring Fee. It also explicitly describes trading lives with friends or teammates, which is a resource exchange creating reciprocity. The 9-diamond complaint concerns customer-service compensation and a game element failing to appear within a move limit; it does not by itself establish a listed dark-pattern mechanic. The statement that players do not have to pay to win denies rather than describes Pay to Progress or Pay to Win.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_RecurringFee",
      "span": "don't buy from this game beyond the pass",
      "rule_applied": "Battle passes, MMO-subscriptions [indicators]",
      "rationale": "The review identifies an in-game pass as a paid product; Fishdom's pass is a season/gold pass. ([uk.trustpilot.com](https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/www.fishdom.com?page=7&utm_source=openai))"
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Reciprocity",
      "span": "Get friends and a team and trade lives.",
      "rule_applied": "Feeling obligated to return a favor, share resources, trade an item, etc.",
      "rationale": "Trading lives is an explicit exchange of resources with other players, matching the reciprocity indicator."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": true,
  "search_query": "Fishdom \"the pass\" 2023 game pass",
  "search_result": "The search established that Fishdom uses a season/gold pass, resolving the review's reference to \"the pass\" as a pass-based purchase. ([uk.trustpilot.com](https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/www.fishdom.com?page=7&utm_source=openai))"
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes two current mechanics. First, lives are regenerated over real time, and the request for a new life within 5-10 minutes implies that the existing regeneration wait is longer, making continued play depend on the game's timer. Second, the game provides daily prizes and resets the player's daily-prize progress when a day is missed. The review does not describe repetitive actions required for progress, a progression gate tied to the daily cycle, or any other codable mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_PlayingByAppointment",
      "span": "maybe only 5-10 minutes for a new life",
      "rule_applied": "Wait to Play: in-game timers that impose an arbitrary wait before something becomes available; the span implies timed life regeneration.",
      "rationale": "The request implies that obtaining another life is controlled by a real-time regeneration timer, requiring the player to wait before resuming play."
    },
    {
      "label": "T_DailyRewards",
      "span": "just because you miss a day doesnt mean that you need to start over on your daily prizes",
      "rule_applied": "Daily log-in reward calendars or resetting daily rewards, including forfeiting progress when a day is missed.",
      "rationale": "The game offers daily prizes and resets the player's daily-prize progress after a missed day."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes an in-game advertisement that cannot be dismissed: there is no close control, taps on the ad redirect to the store, and returning to the game leaves the ad screen active until the app is terminated. This explicitly describes compelled advertisement viewing and an interface that obstructs the opt-out while steering the player toward the store. No progress loss is mentioned, so Mandatory Marathon does not apply.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_Advertisement",
      "span": "there is no way to close it",
      "rule_applied": "definition; compelled to view advertisements",
      "rationale": "The player is forced to remain on the advertisement because it cannot be closed."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_UIMisdirection",
      "span": "if you try to click anywhere on the screen it takes you to store",
      "rule_applied": "boundary rule vs UI complaint; interface obstructs an opt-out and directs attention or action toward a purchase",
      "rationale": "The ad interface removes a safe dismissal path and routes taps toward the store instead."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a current retention mechanic: deleting the game would cause the player to forfeit accumulated in-game purchases and hard-earned progress. This makes leaving costly because the player does not want to lose what they have already invested. The request to add saving and the future intention to spend money are suggestions or plans, not separate current mechanics, so they are not coded. No bug or technical fault is blamed.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_EasyToGetHardToLose",
      "span": "if I deleted the game I would lose everything my in-game purchases and my hard work I really don't want that to happen",
      "rule_applied": "Invested (Endowed) Value; definition of accumulated investment making it difficult to abandon the game",
      "rationale": "Deleting the game would forfeit purchased items and accumulated progress, making the player's existing investment costly to leave behind."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
